This is an in-progress asynchronous multi-tenant API exercise. It is not
production-ready; several modules are still incomplete.

The project uses SQLAlchemy's async API and Pydantic settings. The database URL
is read from `DATABASE_URL`, which defaults to in-memory SQLite for local
development. Copy `.env.example` to `.env` to configure it locally. Never put
database credentials in source code or commit a `.env` file.

Project Structure

text
tenant_api/
│
├── app/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── config.py       # Environment settings
│   ├── database.py     # SQLAlchemy Async Engine & Session
│   ├── models.py       # Database ORM models
│   ├── schemas.py      # Pydantic v2 data contracts
│   ├── services.py     # Decoupled business logic (Tenant scoped)
│   ├── dependencies.py # Secure dependency injection
│   └── router.py       # API endpoints / Controllers
│
└── main.py             # App entrypoint & Middleware

## Configuration

```powershell
Copy-Item .env.example .env
```

Edit `DATABASE_URL` in `.env` when you need a different database. The root
`.gitignore` excludes `.env` files; keep real credentials in environment
variables or a local ignored `.env` file.